BND-04: book the pollutant mass carried by an outfall's reverse flow

The system-outflow pass books the flow an outfall sends into the network
as external inflow, but not the pollutant mass that flow carries, so mass
entered the network without appearing in the quality mass balance. Book
-q_sys * conc alongside the flow, as the 5.3.0 patch does. The only place
that booked it before, for reverse flow into an active LID storage node in
accumulateLinkLoads(), now books it twice, so that line is removed. The
concentrations computed by the model do not change.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-04_swmm600.patch

